WEBVTT

00:00:00.453 --> 00:00:07.253
In this video, we'll take a tour of the CMS, so you know where everything is before you add anything.

00:00:07.827 --> 00:00:11.480
After signing in, you land on the dashboard.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.472
At the top are two tabs.

00:00:13.472 --> 00:00:19.947
Contents holds everything you write, and Media holds the site's shared images.

00:00:20.539 --> 00:00:27.539
Next to them are two links that open in a new tab: the Editor's Handbook, and these video guides.

00:00:28.097 --> 00:00:36.993
On the left are the collections: Site Settings, Topics, FAQs, Videos, Glossary and Comments.

00:00:36.993 --> 00:00:40.377
Each one holds one kind of content.

00:00:40.965 --> 00:00:47.445
At the top right are Quick add, for starting something new from anywhere, and your account menu.

00:00:48.002 --> 00:00:51.070
Click a collection to see its entries.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:52.362
Let's open FAQs.

00:00:52.914 --> 00:00:55.843
Every collection has the same controls.

00:00:55.843 --> 00:00:58.773
The button at the top adds a new entry.

00:00:58.773 --> 00:01:01.177
Below it, each row is one entry.

00:01:01.177 --> 00:01:02.754
Click one to open it.

00:01:03.374 --> 00:01:10.574
Sort by changes the order of the list, and these two buttons switch between a list and a grid.

00:01:11.127 --> 00:01:14.213
The search box finds entries by their words.

00:01:14.213 --> 00:01:16.948
As you type, a menu asks where to look.

00:01:16.948 --> 00:01:20.033
Choose All Collections to search everything.

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:22.979
Each result says which collection it's in.

00:01:22.979 --> 00:01:27.607
Pressing Enter instead searches only the collection you have open.

00:01:28.162 --> 00:01:34.362
Quick add starts a new topic, FAQ, video or glossary term, wherever you are.

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:37.777
Clicking an entry opens the editor.

00:01:37.777 --> 00:01:39.866
On the left are the fields.

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:44.430
Each has a short hint underneath that says what goes in it.

00:01:44.988 --> 00:01:49.121
On the right is a preview of the entry, updated as you type.

00:01:49.121 --> 00:01:53.530
It shows the content and its formatting, but it is only a guide.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:57.388
Always check the real page on the site after publishing.

00:01:57.944 --> 00:02:03.384
These two buttons hide the preview, and keep both sides scrolling together.

00:02:03.936 --> 00:02:07.198
Under the collection name is the save status.

00:02:07.198 --> 00:02:11.619
Changes saved, in green, means everything on screen is saved.

00:02:11.619 --> 00:02:17.200
Unsaved changes, in red, means you've changed something that isn't saved yet.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:21.404
If you try to leave then, the browser asks if you're sure.

00:02:21.404 --> 00:02:24.376
Choose Cancel to stay and keep your work.

00:02:24.941 --> 00:02:32.608
At the top right, the Published menu offers Duplicate, a copy to start a similar entry from.

00:02:32.608 --> 00:02:34.941
And Delete entry removes it.

00:02:34.941 --> 00:02:36.941
We'll use both later on.

00:02:37.495 --> 00:02:41.735
To go back to the list, click the arrow next to the collection name.

00:02:42.451 --> 00:02:48.171
Next: adding an FAQ, from the first word to checking it on the site.
